[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The behaviour model is data, and the writer interprets it

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-SEMANTICS-MODEL-IS-DATA
TITLE: The behaviour model is data, and the writer interprets it
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: The real model, once shaped, needs more than about twelve predicate operations, or a gate whose body cannot be data. At that point the interpreter has become a rule engine and the engine question reopens with EV-SEMANTICS-ENGINE-ALTERNATIVES as the baseline.
STATEMENT: >>>
The behaviour model is one neutral JSON document, and the writer interprets
it. The document holds every lifecycle (its subject, its field, its states in
presentation order, its initial and terminal states, its transitions with
trigger, from, to, gates, writes and emits), every gate as a predicate built
from a CLOSED table of operations, the actors, the commands and events, the
relation contracts, the checkpoints with what each sees, the flows, and the
rules that are still prose. A small interpreter the repository owns, standard
library only, loads and validates the document, preflights a command against
its gates, applies the write on a staged copy of the graph, ripples the
emitted events to a fixed point in a deterministic order, and commits the
whole change or refuses all of it. The eval-time diagnostics and the mermaid
rendering are functions over the document.

No third-party lifecycle engine sits underneath, and transitions leaves both
Nix delivery sites. A rule is never Python: a rule that fits an existing
operation is data only, and a new operation is a small addition to the closed
table with its own tests. The size of that table is what this decision
watches.

The document's shape is the target SLICE-BEHAVIOUR-MODEL's typed Nix option
surface emits. Until that surface exists the document is committed by hand in
the same shape, so the emitter later replaces the hand-written file and a
check proves the two equal, the way strictdoc-grammar-model-equal does for the
grammar. The Python interpreter is the only interpreter: the Nix side types
the model, cross-checks it against the grammar and emits it; it does not
evaluate gates.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
From EV-SEMANTICS-ENGINE-ALTERNATIVES. No library handles the whole
vocabulary. The statechart libraries (transitions, python-statemachine,
XState) carry the ladder, the branch and the diagram and nothing else: in each
of them a gate body is code, a method name, a callable or a JavaScript
function, so the rows that broke the spike (a gate that sees the graph, a
comparison across an edge, the ripple, checkpoints, relation contracts) are
caller code whichever library is underneath, and a Nix emitter could not
target them either way. The engines that do express every row (clingo, OPA,
pySHACL) do it as rule text in a second language, which under DEC-LAYER-STACK
is a rule living in a script body, and bring a second evaluation model; two of
the three showed measured defects in their probes. Two probes run separately,
the Nix option-tree probe and the no-library baseline, converged on the same
shape: a JSON model with a closed predicate vocabulary and a fixed interpreter
of a few hundred lines. That is the only shape where DEC-LAYER-STACK holds by
construction rather than by discipline, because there is no module a rule
could be written into.

transitions itself is dormant (2 commits in 12 months, 1 release in 24, no
maintainer reply on any 2026 issue or pull request) and its nixpkgs package
propagates pygraphviz unconditionally, a 312 MB closure at both delivery sites
for a backend that is never imported. Adopting the data shape subtracts a
dependency instead of adding one.

What it costs. The repository owns a few hundred lines with no upstream to
find bugs; the baseline probe surfaced two defects in its own interpreter,
both caught only by negative controls, so the tests carry the burden a library
would. Three things no candidate supplied and this shape must build: a
transaction (refuse the whole change, never half of it), termination (a step
bound and a visited set, so a cyclic model refuses instead of hanging), and
validation on load (every state, gate, operation and lifecycle reference
resolves, or the document is rejected).

Rejected. Keep transitions and add a graph layer beside it: the layer would
own most of the vocabulary while the library held three rows, and the library
is dormant. Swap to python-statemachine: healthy and loads JSON, but its loader
silently disables three diagnostics, a refused send raises nothing, and
checkpoints and contracts stay outside it. A lifecycle engine plus a
graph-query engine: pySHACL needs an RDF projection of the corpus and cannot
reach a fixed point across shapes; clingo and OPA are a second language with a
second evaluator.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Open, not accepted. Written 2026-09-03 by the session that ran the assessment.
The operator delegated the pick ("pick the path or reject a pivot") and
confirms or rejects it here.

Questions the evidence cannot settle, carried verbatim from the synthesis for
the operator:

- Does a hand-written rule library in a second language satisfy
  DEC-LAYER-STACK? A 214-line Nix engine and a 318-line Python interpreter are
  also machinery. Where is the line? This decision reads the line as: data
  plus a fixed interpreter is inside it; rule text in a second language is
  not.
- How many distinct gate shapes does the real model need, versus gate
  instances? Probes used three to eight predicate operations; the real number
  is unknown, and the RETIRES_ON condition is where that number bites.
- Does the write path need a per-write gate, or is checkpoint granularity
  enough? This decision assumes a per-write gate in the daemon, in-process and
  under a millisecond, because scribe is the only writer.
- Does a refused ripple roll back the write that triggered it? This decision
  says yes: the staged copy is committed whole or not at all.
- May the board consume a different representation than the daemon? This
  decision says no: the board reads the same emitted payload.
- Does corpus-scale performance need measuring before or after? After, on the
  interpreter that exists; WORK-SEMANTICS-CORPUS-SCALE-MEASURE.
- Is DEC-DEPS-VIA-NIX binding? It is open too. This decision does not need it:
  the data shape adds no dependency under either reading.
<<<
